  "objective": "Cross-chain settlement integrity, hardest first: (1) IMDRetroWall.ccipReceive: router, source chain selector and sender checks, winnerIndex = randomWord % ticketCount(epoch), claimable[winner] += prize, then pull-based claimReward(). (2) requestSettlement(epoch): exact-fee InsufficientFee revert, SETTLEMENT_RETRY_DELAY = 1 day, and the SettlementStatus Requested/Settled machine must prevent double settlement or re-request at the epoch boundary. (3) VrfCcipRelay on Base: ccipReceive validation, _deliver when the word is cached, rawFulfillRandomWords first-word-wins and the UnknownRequest guard, and permissionless deliver(epoch) must not send a stale/zero word or replay a delivered epoch. (4) ERC-165 supportsInterface for IAny2EVMMessageReceiver (0x85572ffb) must not revert for unknown ids or 0xffffffff, because the off-ramp silently downgrades such receivers to token-only no-ops. (5) Economic bounds: MAX_STAMPS_PER_EPOCH = 5, 500 burn / 500 pool, stranded funds (no sweep). Current pair: wall 0x9550E4F888d1C084CB1C8E74677Da54109723EE3 (Robinhood 4663), relay 0x887bbed753938087Ce61Ca768a358848177E6eaA (Base 8453). Audited commit a5c1af9.",
